species level mycorrhizal state updates for the FRED 4.0 subset

iteration 01
------------

- extracted mycorrhizal states from FRED 4.0 (the whole dataset) (had multiple entries per species, for many species).
- extracted mycorrhizal states from Maherali et. al. 2016.
- extracted mycorrhizal states from FungalRoot species level dataset (had multiple entries per species, for many species).
- wherever a species had multiple and conflicting state info in FRED 4.0 and FungalRoot species level dataset, it was resolved 
  manually by combining states where it was intuitive (AM & EcM into EcMAM, AM & NM into NMAM).
- where this combination was less intuitive (i.e. when the resultant state is not very common), FungalRoot genus level state recommendations were used.
- once the hand cleanup was over, merged all together to create a single dataset.
- had 264 state missing species.

iteration 02
--------------

- scraped and parsed the Table 1 in (Wang and Qiu, 2006) from Springer's site.
- Wang & Qiu 2006 has no species overlap with the species we needed state data for. No longer entertaining it.
- when (Brundrett & Tedersoo 2018) did not have the needed family, FungalRoot species level dataset (Soudzilovskaia et al., 2020) was used to find the state info (genus level recommendations).
- the new column named state_revision_1 contains all the original state data and the new states from the said sources.
- the rows of state_revision_1 where revision_1_source column isn't empty are the newly updated states.
- once this was done, families with more than one mycorrhizal states were cross checked with (Brundrett & Tedersoo 2018) and (Soudzilovskaia et al., 2020).
  corrections were done where necessary and these were included in the column state_revision_2 and their corresponding sources are in the column revision_2_source

